; Maze 2 descriptor (4 words)
;
; Maze 2 descriptor: four words giving the maze's wrap delta and its starting positions (8 bytes, MAZE_DESC_SIZE). The
; maze is selected by the maze number 1 in #R$7C63 (numbers run 0 to 3 and repeat, the game starts with maze 0), and
; the descriptor is copied by #R$6A9E to the current maze descriptor #R$6FCF when #R$6000 starts the maze. It goes
; with the map #R$6FF7 (Maze2Map); the four descriptors are at #R$6FD7, #R$6FDF, #R$6FE7 and #R$6FEF but their maps
; are not in the same order in memory.
; .
; Fields:
; +0 word: vertical wrap delta, added to the position of Horace or a guard that goes up through a wrap pad (tile 9 of
;   the map) and subtracted when going down: a screen-offset difference (#R$6337, #R$63DA); 0 when the maze has no
;   wrap pads
; +2 word: position of the bell at the start of the maze (copied to #R$7CC4; 0 there means no bell)
; +4 word: position of the first guard when its release timer is zero (guard 1 at the start of a maze)
; +6 word: position of Horace's start, at the left-hand arrows; a guard whose release timer is not zero waits here too
; Positions are screen offsets (address minus $4000) of the top-left cell of a 2x2-cell block: THIRD_SIZE per screen
; third of 8 character rows, CELL_ROW_STEP per row inside a third, plus the column.
;
@label=Maze2Desc
@isub=DEFW THIRD_SIZE*2+CELL_ROW_STEP*3
b$6FDF DEFW $1060 ; wrap delta: 19 character rows
@isub=DEFW CELL_ROW_STEP*7+28
 $6FE1 DEFW $00FC ; bell: row 7, column 28
@isub=DEFW THIRD_SIZE*2+16
 $6FE3 DEFW $1010 ; guard 1 start: row 16, column 16
@isub=DEFW THIRD_SIZE+CELL_ROW_STEP*2+1
 $6FE5 DEFW $0841 ; Horace start: row 10, column 1
